00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.043
- Manny was like angry, yapping and,

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:03.795
and this and that. I'm in the bathroom.

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:04.796
-  Oh, you were in the bathroom
when that happened?

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:05.672
- I was in the bathroom.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.465
When I came out the brawl was already...

00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:11.886
Because I'm zipping up my pants quickly 
and I’m trying to get to see what’s going on.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:14.973
And I see Zimmer rushing towards
me and I'm like, “What?”

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:19.144
He got close to me, said some bad
words. He actually tried to jab me. 

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:28.695
♪♪♪

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.613
- [Master Tesfatsion]: So who
we got in the pool hall today?

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:32.615
Pedro Martinez. What's good, baby?
- [Pedro Martínez]: Ay.

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:33.616
All right, all right.

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:34.242
- How you livin'?

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:38.621
- I'm livin' great. Watching you, ready
to play some pool, I'm excited.

00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:40.248
Let's get it on, boy.

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:42.792
I haven’t played in a very, very, very long time. 

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:43.877
- You got it.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.296
[Balls hitting. Ball dropping into pocket]

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:47.088
- You got one in.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.673
- I got one in. I got lucky.

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:50.842
- Pedro, you're one of my favorite
baseball players of all time.

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:54.846
I love the fiery aggression
that you played with.

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:56.931
It was just so relatable for me,
growing up with nothing

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.767
and having that kind of
anger growing up as a kid.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.226
Where did that come from?

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:04.230
- Well it’s a long story man but,
uh, our family was a big family.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.317
 Thanks to God, Ramón led the way.

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:10.278
Ramón was still bouncing
in the minor leagues.

00:01:10.278 --> 00:01:14.157
It’s a little later for the LA Dodgers.
Didn’t make any money yet.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:18.620
Mom and dad were left at home with
me and the rest of the kids and uh-

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.872
I was dropped at the
Academy really early.

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:21.539
- What age?

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:25.126
- Fourteen-and-a-half, fifteen?
Because I was quick to fight.

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:26.586
- [Laughing]

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.504
I can relate.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:29.547
- [Laughing]

00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:33.468
I was really quick to fight. Any picking on
one of my cousins would be my fight.

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:36.930
Family members, uh, friends.
That would be my fight. 

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:39.390
There you go. 

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.183
- He gonna beat my ass.

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:41.518
- [Laughing]

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:42.977
I mean, I think most
people remember,

00:01:42.977 --> 00:01:46.606
from an anger perspective,
the 2003 ALCS.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.024
- It’s that Zimmer incident.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:48.691
- What happened?

00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:53.154
- Well, I threw a ball behind Karim
García and my shoulder was hurting.

00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:56.699
And I had men on first and second.
Karim García's the ninth place hitter,

00:01:56.699 --> 00:02:00.078
and I'm trying to rush a
fastball up and in on him,

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:01.955
but I did it out of the slide step.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:07.043
And I took the ball. I'm dragging.
I'm tired. I'm aching.

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:10.088
You can't let the opposition
know that your shoulder hurts.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.173
- That's food. They'll eat you up.

00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:14.384
- Exactly. So, the ball
came behind him, and

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:17.637
instead of in front of him,
up here, came behind him.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.848
So, and when he ducked
down the ball hit the bat.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:22.517
It looks like the ball is over his head.
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:26.396
- So Zimmer took obsession to that.
They started yapping this and that.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:29.566
I continue to pitch, got a
ground ball, double play,

00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:33.069
but when Karim García is going to second
he almost kills the second baseman.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:36.656
He was sliding to second and
took my second baseman out.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.991
I just said, “What are you thinking?”

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:41.411
 It's a 2 to 1 game or a 3
to 2, something like that.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:44.914
“Who wants to hit you?
You crazy? Clean it up.”

00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:49.419
So Posada popped up, Zimmer popped
up. Everybody started yapping on me.

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:53.548
But I went in, got the inning done. Roger
Clemens throws the ball at Manny.

00:02:53.548 --> 00:02:55.383
- Manny Ramírez.
- And then- 

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.218
- Manny wasn't gonna take that.

00:02:57.218 --> 00:03:01.014
- Manny was like angry, yapping and,
and this and that. I'm in the bathroom.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:01.931
- Oh, you were in the bathroom
when that happened?

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:04.726
- I was in the bathroom.
So I came out a little later.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:08.938
When I came out the brawl was already...
Because I'm zipping up my pants quickly and,

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:11.566
and I'm trying to get to
see what's going on.

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:14.861
And that's when I hear the
mumbling, kind of behind me.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:18.781
And I see Zimmer rushing towards
me, and I'm like, “What?”

00:03:18.781 --> 00:03:21.868
And that's when he got close
to me, said some bad words

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.828
that I didn't expect
from Zimmer either.

00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.955
He actually tried to jab me.

00:03:25.955 --> 00:03:29.626
So I pulled it, and that's why
it looks like I grabbed him.

00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:34.088
But in reality, that's the only blemish I
would love to erase from my career.

00:03:34.088 --> 00:03:37.634
There hasn't been any other
moment where I felt worse

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:40.220
in my life. I was- I will tell you my life,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.181
than that moment. And that
moment led to a lot more.

00:03:43.181 --> 00:03:44.057
- Go ahead, take a shot.

00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:47.518
Oo, we got the touch there.

00:03:47.518 --> 00:03:49.604
- Yeah there you go.
- [Laughing]

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:51.522
So when you go back to New
York now what is it like?

00:03:51.522 --> 00:03:54.400
- You know what, it's a lot better
than, than I ever thought.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.904
People really realize
what I did, how I did it.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.322
I became a Hall of Famer.

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:01.950
I've done so many other things
that people didn't know.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:06.204
They see that my attitude was
different when I wasn't pitching.

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.081
Like, Nomar tying me to the post.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:08.998
- What happened with that?

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.917
- Well, I was like the lucky charm.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.670
I would come out and I would
last for two or three runs,

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:17.131
they would get the two or three runs
and Nomar was hitting like crazy.

00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:20.593
And that day I had pitch, so I
was running on the treadmill.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.471
I was doing some more
exercises in the clubhouse

00:04:23.471 --> 00:04:27.100
and I hadn't come out and
Nomar was, I guess, 0 for 2.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.727
Nomar did not like that, he went
and grabbed me and goes,

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:31.604
"Ah, you get out here,
you get out here.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.941
You be loud, you do whatever, but
we need to continue to do that."

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.277
And Nomar was really superstitious.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:41.447
So I was so loud all day that even
after we got the game one side,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.825
even Nomar got tired
of me being so loud.

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:47.954
I got to the post and I kept just
yapping and yapping and yapping

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:51.499
and Nomar and Portugal
decided that they had enough

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:55.003
and they tied me up to the post
before I realized what they were doing,

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:58.965
I’m- like tied up with this
heavy tape and I can't move.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.010
Even though I was taped to the
post everybody's laughing

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:05.805
